{
  "requirement": "`habeas_sdk::storage` MUST expose the following helper:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\nuse serde::{Serialize, de::DeserializeOwned};\nuse habeas_sdk::graph::{NodePath, Record};\n\npub struct FileEvidenceStorage { /* private fields */ }\n\npub enum FileStorageError {\n    Io(std::io::Error),\n    Json(serde_json::Error),\n}\n\nimpl FileEvidenceStorage {\n    pub fn new(root: impl Into<PathBuf>) -> Self;\n\n    pub async fn load<N, M>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n    ) -> Result<Option<Record<N, M>>, FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: DeserializeOwned + Send,\n        M: DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    pub async fn store<N, M>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        record: &Record<N, M>,\n    ) -> Result<(), FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: Serialize + Sync,\n        M: Serialize + Sync;\n}\n```\n\nThe helper MUST be `Send + Sync`, and its load and store futures MUST be `Send`.\nConstruction MUST retain the supplied root without performing filesystem I/O.\nThe SDK's `Record`, `Dependency`, `Fingerprint`, and `Judgment` types MUST\nsupport Serde serialization and deserialization when their type parameters do.\nThese bounds MUST NOT be imposed on `Graph` or `EvidenceStorage` themselves.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no adequacy gap. The tests cover each obligation of `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface`. I did not read the implementation.\n\n- **Exposed API.** `FileEvidenceStorage::new`, `load` and `store` are called with the stated generic bounds throughout `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs`. Both `FileStorageError::Io` and `FileStorageError::Json` are matched. In `records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error`, `Json` comes from malformed content and from loading as `u8`. `Io` comes from a directory sitting at the record path. In `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys`, `Io` also comes from an over-long key.\n- **`Send + Sync` helper and `Send` futures.**\n  - `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys` wraps `store.store(..)` and `store.load(..)` in `send<T: Send>`. The compiler therefore checks that both futures are `Send`.\n  - `concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes` shares an `Arc<FileEvidenceStorage>` across `std::thread::scope` threads. That compiles only if the helper is `Send + Sync`.\n  - `checker_needs_no_validation_and_storage_preserves_nonserializable_metadata` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs` also uses `send(..)` on the graph storage futures.\n- **Construction retains the root and does no I/O.**\n  - `paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects` builds a store on a nonexistent root. It asserts that `record_path` equals `root.join(expected)` for several paths, which shows the root is retained. It asserts that the root still does not exist after the loads.\n  - `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys` asserts `!root.exists()` right after construction.\n- **Serde support for `Record`, `Dependency`, `Fingerprint` and `Judgment`.**\n  - The `record()` helper builds both `Dependency::Node` and `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` variants, each with a `Fingerprint`, plus a `Judgment` with metadata.\n  - The round-trip test stores that record, loads it back, and asserts equality of `procedure`, `dependencies` and `output`. That is a real serialize and deserialize check.\n  - Loading with `N = u8` yields a `Json` error. This shows the node type parameter takes part in deserialization.\n- **No Serde bounds on `Graph` or `EvidenceStorage`.** `checker_needs_no_validation_and_storage_preserves_nonserializable_metadata` uses `Node` and `Metadata` types that deliberately have no Hash, Serde or Display bounds. It implements the graph and evidence storage over them and runs store, load and check. That compiling and passing demonstrates the bounds are absent from those traits.\n\nEach test carries a `{test}` reference to the subject. The behaviors it names are exercised and asserted.",
  "references": "6de22a4662b3b56e1ca0c5c967c7bc2bffab534cc735b328c21e2f366f729613",
